coordination remain active in the field. On August 27th to 28th, Earth Shadow will cover 96% of the moon's face during a near total event. Observers in North and South America will see the longest phase of the eclipse according to reports from fizz.org space. The geometry places the Americas in the best viewing zone compared with other continents. No total coverage is expected, yet the depth of the partial phase will still darken the lunar disk noticeably.

